/** Provides on-screen gamepads for phones: sticks a finger works, read through raylib's gamepad functions. Imported apart, with its
	constants: `import helix.raylib.extras.VirtualGamepad.*;`.

	The first touch anywhere on the screen plugs an enabled virtual gamepad in. A mouse click leaves the virtual gamepad unplugged. Once
	the virtual gamepad is plugged in, `IsGamepadAvailable` is true for its slot, and its sticks read through `GetGamepadAxisMovement`.
	`IsGamepadVirtual` tells a virtual gamepad from a physical one.

	A physical gamepad plugged into the virtual gamepad's slot replaces the virtual gamepad. The first physical gamepad plugged in takes
	slot 0. The next touch after the physical gamepad is unplugged plugs the virtual gamepad in again.

	Every finger is a free finger until a stick takes it. A free finger counts as the mouse, as every finger does without a virtual
	gamepad. The touch functions list every finger.

	The virtual gamepad is drawn at `EndDrawing`, over everything the frame drew. The virtual gamepad is hidden while a physical gamepad
	is in its slot.

	```haxe
	InitWindow(800, 450, "twin stick");
	EnableVirtualGamepad(0);
	while (!WindowShouldClose()) {
		var moveX = GetGamepadAxisMovement(0, GAMEPAD_AXIS_LEFT_X);
